[[Lieutenant]] '''Noum''', [[MD]] was a [[Tellarite]] [[sciences division]] [[Starfleet]] [[lieutenant]] who served as [[chief medical officer]] on the {{USS|Dauntless|NCC-80816}} and later as [[ship's counselor]] on the {{USS|Voyager|NCC-74656-A|-A}}.

== Service history ==
=== USS ''Dauntless'' ===
He was on the [[bridge]] in [[2384]] when the ''Dauntless''{{'}}s [[sensor]]s detected a third [[proto-warp signature]] originating from the {{USS|Protostar}}. ({{PRO|A Moral Star, Part 2}})

He later joined the [[away team]] that discovered [[the Diviner]] at [[Tars Lamora]]. ({{PRO|Asylum}}) Following the discovery, he attempted to revive the Diviner. He managed to do so when [[Ensign]] [[Asencia]] suggested that the fluid in the patient's exosuit could be a kind of bio-serum for his species ({{PRO|Let Sleeping Borg Lie}}).

Noum was on the bridge when the ''Protostar'' suddenly emerged right in front of the ''Dauntless'', then took off at high warp. Tysess immediately called the Admiral to report to bridge, but Noum stated she was not answering comms, leading Tysess to wonder where she was since they needed her immediately. When Tysess asked if they could get closer to the ''Protostar''. Ensign Asencia suggested that they could close the gap if they rerouted power from [[quantum slipstream]]--that would allow them to merge their [[warp field]]s and lock onto their course. When Noum argued that if the Protostar engaged their [[proto-engine]], they'd be torn apart. Asencia pointed out that the proto-drive was offline and reminded Tysess that the Admiral did not want them to lose the ship.

When Admiral Janeway finally reported to the bridge, she displayed highly erratic behavior, leading Noum to order her to drink a cup of [[coffee]]. When Janeway immediately spit the coffee out, Noum realized something was wrong. He went to her [[ready room]] and insisted that she come to [[sickbay]] for tests, telling her that he ran a scan on her and found some damage in her [[cerebral cortex]]. The admiral declined by literally throwing Noum out of her ready room. She then quickly left the bridge after putting Tysess (whom she referred to in this instance as "antenna") in charge.

Afterwards, Noum, Tysess and Ascencia found Janeway in her quarters, dancing erratically. When Tysess informed her that they were taking her to sickbay, Janeway made a run for it but was quickly subdued by members of her crew. When a furious Janeway asked "Don't you know who I am?" Noum replied that, no, they did not, sedated her, and had her placed in sickbay in restraints for her own protection.

Later, on the bridge, it was discovered that Janeway, in an [[environmental suit]] was walking along the outside of the ''Dauntless''. Tysess demanded that she be [[beam]]ed back, but Noum stated that the merged warp field made that impossible. While Tysess insisted that they find an option before she burned herself alive, Noum complained that she was endangering the lives of everyone aboard the ship. Ultimately, they were able to pull the admiral back in with a [[tractor beam]] and have her placed in the [[brig]]. ({{PRO|Mindwalk}})

=== USS ''Voyager''-A ===
Following the ''Protostar''{{'}}s destruction, Noum transferred to the {{USS|Voyager|NCC-74656-A|-A}} to serve as the ship's [[Counselor]] under [[The Doctor]]. He refused to let warrant officer [[Dal R'El]] and his group onto the bridge. Noum, Janeway, and Tysess then spoke about Admiral [[Edward Jellico]]'s orders about abandoning the covert rescue of Captain Chakotay using the ''{{dis|Infinity|ship}}''. Noum and Tysses were ready to disobey orders along with Janeway and prepped it for launch. However, Dal, [[Jankom Pog]], [[Zero]] and [[Maj'el]] left earlier than planned aboard the ''Infinity''. ({{PRO|Into the Breach, Part I|Into the Breach, Part II|Who Saves the Saviors}})

Following the failed rescue, Noum agreed with the Doctor that the ''Protostar'' crew were dysfunctional troublemakers like the {{USS|Cerritos}}' crew. He also wondered how the orb knew of their mission. Noum and the crew did not want to end the rescue mission this way. Following the wormhole's closure, Noum noticed that {{dis|Jankom Pog|hologram|Hologram Jankom}} was using a napkin and studying in the mess hall. ({{PRO|Observer's Paradox|The Fast and the Curious}})

Noum and Janeway's officers realized that Dal and his group had created holographic duplicates of themselves when they discovered {{dis|Gwyndala|hologram|Gwyn's hologram}} following an unknown attack that froze time. He supported Janeway's decision to enter a [[Transwarp aperture]] despite Jellico's orders. However, he hid behind several crates in the shuttlebay during the [[Loom]]'s attack before he was found by cadets {{dis|Zeph|2384}} and [[Grom]]. ({{PRO|The Devourer of All Things, Part I|The Devourer of All Things, Part II}})

Following the Loom's attack and [[Wesley Crusher]]'s disappearance, Noum was able call in a few favors at [[Starfleet Medical]] in order for Janeway to speak with his mother, Dr. [[Beverly Crusher]]. He then welcomed Chakotay and his crew back to ''Voyager'' and was amazed that they went to the [[mirror universe]]. ({{PRO|Last Flight of the Protostar, Part II|Cracked Mirror}})

During the ''Rev''-1's initial attack, Noum treated the injured Grom's arm. He and the Doctor then examined Commander [[Tysess]] after ''Voyager''-A was breached by the [[Incursor]]. They saw that Tysess was dying of "old age" due to the weapon's [[temporal radiation]]. Following the attack, Noum and the rest of Janeway's senior staff supported her decision to rescue [[Ilthuran]] from [[Asencia]]. ({{PRO|Ascension, Part I|Ascension, Part II|Brink}})

When ''Voyager'' escorted the ''Protostar'' through the wormhole back in time, Noum manned one of the bridge consoles as did the Doctor. Noum reported that navigation was down, but Janeway was able to compensate by having [[Gillian]] plot them a course from [[Cetacean Ops]]. Later, Noum and Tysess listened to Jankom animatedly tell a story that amused them both. ({{PRO|Ouroboros, Part II}})

== Holograms {{anchor|Holograms}} ==
Following [[Jankom Pog]]'s encounter with Noum, he created a [[holodeck]] scenario featuring the doctor, who appeared in the form of five [[motorcycle]]-riding [[hooligan]]s, with whom he fought in a [[street fighting sim]].

When the [[living construct]] caused [[Hologram Janeway]] to take over the ''Protostar'' and trap the crew in the holodeck, a number of [[holoprogram]]s used by the crew merged, and Noum to appeared in various scenarios, first as five bikers from Pog's sim. One of the bikers had a [[Key Club]] [[tattoo]] on his {{dis|chest|anatomy}}.

